.TH FUTAB 1 "November 2026" "FuTab" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
futab \- guitar tablature viewer, editor and player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B futab
.RB [ \-\-safe\-mode ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B futab
shows guitar tablature and standard notation in a window, in four layouts,
and exports it to PDF.
With
.I file
it opens that file when it starts.
.PP
FuTab is a fork of OxiGuitar.
It opens and saves files only through format plugins, single files
ending in
.IR .oxp ,
and uses OxiGuitar's plugins: the package
.B oxiguitar\-guitarpro
opens Guitar Pro files of every version from 3 to 8 (.gp3, .gp4, .gp5,
\&.gpx, .gp).
With no format plugin installed, nothing can be opened, and the footer says
where to get plugins.
A plugin is loaded only when it is first needed.
.PP
.B Tools \(-> Plugins
lists the plugins found, with their versions, and enables or disables each
one from the next start.
.B Help \(-> About
lists the plugin folders in the order they are searched.
.PP
FuTab sends nothing over the network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-safe\-mode
Start without using any plugin.
The plugin manager still lists them, so a plugin that keeps FuTab from
working can be disabled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/futab/settings.json
The settings, created as
.B {}
on the first start.
.B plugin_folders
replaces the folders searched for plugins, and
.B disabled
lists the plugins not to use.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/futab/plugins/
Your own plugins, created on the first start.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/futab/plugins/
FuTab's own plugins, installed by packages.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/oxiguitar/plugins/
OxiGuitar's plugins, installed by its packages; searched after FuTab's.
FuTab only reads these folders.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Replaces
.I ~/.config
in the path of the settings.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Replaces
.I ~/.local/share
in the path of your plugin folder.
.TP
.B OXIGUITAR_HOME
One folder for the settings and your plugins, in place of both above.
.TP
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY ", " DISPLAY
The display to open the window on.
The
.B futab
package is the Wayland build; on a desktop without Wayland, install
.B \%futab\-x11
instead.
A build started where it can't open a window says which build is needed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the window is closed; 1 if it could not be opened.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/PurpleIcon/futab/issues
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR futab\-cli (1)
.PP
